A constant template is finished during compilation.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    title #= "Moth"

    heading #= [$md:
        # [title]
    ]
]

A bare direct [$html:<code>&#91;...&#93;</code>] in `@entry.moth` must fold at compile time. An
explicit [$html:<code>~&#91;...&#93;</code>] instead creates a runtime body fragment, even if foldable.
The removed direct [$html:<code>#&#91;...&#93;</code>] spelling is invalid. The entry file's presence
selects the page. A direct const root `$in` insert supplies builder
metadata, while an ordinary const fragment renders into the body.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    [$in title:About]
    [$in stylesheets:[@assets/site.css]]

    [$md:
        # Compile-time heading
    ]
]

Only a direct root insert reaches builder routing. Nested and stored inserts
remain ordinary template composition. Scalar builder values concatenate, and
each stylesheet insert needs one tracked CSS resource. The HTML builder
deduplicates stylesheets by resource origin.

Runtime top-level named builder inserts are not supported.

Assigned or returned templates remain ordinary values, not direct page fragments.

Const template loops have an iteration limit so an accidental build-time loop
cannot run forever.
